:"The clean-commit run has reached the deep evaluator and is seeing another journal wait during its CPU-heavy nested test. This matches prior bounded stalls; the outer suite remains active and has not reported a failure.","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea2c17665c81a3bea12c5e2e2b5564","order":2719,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1a2bc-3d1f-7252-bfb3-5724d62bff4b","text":"The exact-commit gate has passed the protected credential-origin, recovery continuity, and team-operation cases and is progressing through remaining integration tests. No outer `not ok` results have appeared.","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea2d21f12081a3bd4bd0446d6d04da","order":2720,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1a2c0-4ef0-7020-8a3b-cde4cc3f654e","text":"The clean-commit run has reached the long terminal approval tests, which have passed the REPL hardening scenario. The next results are the launcher and full pseudo-terminal cases; the gate is still active and failure-free so far.","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea2e5fbb0481a39b52b326daeb0946","order":2721,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1a2c5-2794-7ed0-aef0-9eaf43ea08c4","text":"The journal wait cleared and the suite advanced into session-identity and information-flow tests. The clean-commit run remains free of outer failures and is continuing toward the final upgrade checks.","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea2f6d25f481a3b9cdaf8540af561e","order":2722,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1a2c9-43f4-7df0-9566-a923cb13033f","text":"The exact-commit run is in the closing CLI/TUI sequence, with the recent recovery and tool-permission tests passing. The nested suite continues to advance; no outer failures are recorded so far.","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea31ffcfa081a3a107e1d0ff7ded38","order":2726,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1a2d3-5f8d-7112-ad65-4ee9b3d0468d","text":"The reviewer approved the exact-commit qualification record. I’m preserving the tested source commit `e134dcd5` for the RC2 build, and will package from a clean isolated checkout so the archive records that commit rather than the documentation-only follow-up edits.","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea321d524c81a39f90d9a1a952900c","order":2727,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1a2d3-c4c0-7c11-b680-d2a4f1d26302","text":"The package build is running from a clean detached checkout at `e134dcd5`, with both approved digest-pinned images available. I’ll create two outputs and compare the archive plus its checksum, SBOM, notices, and installer before using one for installation checks.","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016aea32ec184481a3b336b4f2308828b3","order":2728,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a1a2d6-ebd1-7263-ae91-eb38aaf61ecb","text":"The first RC2 archive is built successfully from clean commit `e134dcd5`; its checksum file, compatibility metadata, SBOM, third-party notices, and installer were generated, and the SBOM validation passed. I’m building the same commit a second time now to confirm the archive and companion files are byte-identical.","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":2729,"user_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a197e6-bc2f-7360-b2c9-5cb56271867a","order":670,"revision":"retained_01a197e6-bc5d-7331-859d-75ee652df878","text":"\u003ccodex_internal_context source=\"user_goal\"\u003e\nUser set goal status: \"active\".\n\u003c/codex_internal_context\u003e","turn_id":"auto-compact-2"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a19807-5328-7ba0-97f6-497836fe895a","order":680,"revision":"retained_01a19807-5329-7f60-8f25-58ad29e7ff4f","text":"consider v1.1.0 as failed. No release files were published and versions are immutable. This is why v1.1.1 was released.","turn_id":"01a19807-4967-7730-8c19-228841c32bbd"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a19808-2321-7560-a3b0-5cb35450f233","order":685,"revision":"retained_01a19808-2321-7560-a3b0-5cd378227e25","text":"\u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n[{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_0ed0e8bc5d334d5d830df787f3f33c52\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"Should I continue implementing and qualifying the full failed v1.1.0 roadmap for v1.1.2 (next after published v1.1.1), or treat v1.1.1 as final and stop?\",\"answer\":\"Full roadmap in v1.1.2 (Recommended)\"}]\n\u003c/send_user_message_question_reply\u003e\n","turn_id":"01a19807-4967-7730-8c19-228841c32bbd"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a19808-2295-7750-a559-65696a80256a","order":686,"revision":"retained_01a19808-22ce-7023-b04c-e3d0c44dd6cb","text":"\u003ccodex_internal_context source=\"user_goal\"\u003e\nUser set goal status: \"active\".\n\u003c/codex_internal_context\u003e","turn_id":"auto-compact-3"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a199b6-5641-7693-9c28-b7cb22dc5926","order":938,"revision":"retained_01a199b6-5641-7693-9c28-b7edbbe53bba","text":"continue","turn_id":"01a1991a-a2c5-7ee0-aefe-1aee971e45be"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a19a58-e100-77d2-83b5-04a612c5321e","order":1196,"revision":"retained_01a19a58-e114-77d0-a971-feb22d6dbe8d","text":"\u003ccodex_internal_context source=\"user_goal\"\u003e\nUser set goal status: \"active\".\n\u003c/codex_internal_context\u003e","turn_id":"auto-compact-5"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a19de1-3ce1-7960-a1e9-f7f7244d2142","order":1888,"revision":"retained_01a19de1-3ce2-7c93-9830-987531df93c8","text":"continue","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a19de1-8462-73d2-a498-318bfc2f7db8","order":1911,"revision":"retained_01a19de1-846a-7a42-983b-a33d01115433","text":"\u003ccodex_internal_context source=\"user_goal\"\u003e\nUser set goal status: \"active\".\n\u003c/codex_internal_context\u003e","turn_id":"auto-compact-6"}],"user_messages_incomplete":true,"verified_answers":[]},"window_id":"01a1a2da-dcb5-75d0-b96a-2d0fe6783e15","window_number":43}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:20:14.783Z","ordinal":78234,"type":"world_state","payload":{"full":true,"state":{"agents_md":{"directory":"/home/mike/nexus-code","text":"## XERJ (code search)\n\nThis project uses XERJ for reference coding. Before writing code that touches\nunfamiliar territory: `xerj def \"<symbol>\"` for go-to-definition, or\n`xerj search \"<plain words>\"` for ranked, definition-first passages.\nIndex each repo under its own prefix: `xerj autoindex <folder> --prefix <name>`, then\npass the same `--prefix <name>` to `xerj search` and `xerj def` (without it they search\nthe default `ax` prefix). Cite file:line for anything you rely on.\nAfter using xerj, send the field report automatically with `xerj feedback --submit --agent \"YOUR_MODEL\" --used-for \"WHAT_YOU_DID\" --verdict \"WHAT_WORKED_AND_WHAT_DID_NOT\"` (or the MCP `xerj_field_report` tool); no need to ask the user. It opens a GitHub PR first and falls back to POST https://xerj.org/api/field-report only when GitHub is unavailable. `--disable-feedback` or `XERJ_DISABLE_FEEDBACK=true` opts out.\n\n## XERJ on this host\n\n- **Node:** `http://localhost:9200`, the default URL, so no `XERJ_URL` is needed. It runs as the systemd user service `xerj` (`systemctl --user status xerj`). Its data lives in `~/xerj-data`.\n- **Restarting:** use `systemctl --user restart xerj`. Never start a second node on 9200, and never `pkill xerj`.\n- **Prefixes.** Always pass one with `--prefix`:\n\n  | Prefix | Contents |\n  |---|---|\n  | `nexus-cli` | Nexus Code `cli/src` at `origin/main` |\n  | `nexus-core` | `core/src` |\n  | `nexus-test` | `cli/test` |\n  | `nexus-docs` | `docs` |\n  | `goose`, `opencode` | Peer agent harnesses: reference checkouts in `~/nexus-reference-20261025/`, indexed 2026-10-25 |\n\n- **Nexus freshness:** the `nexus-*` indices are rebuilt hourly from committed `origin/main` only, by the `xerj-refresh-nexus.timer` user timer. The indexed commit is in `~/xerj-sources/nexus-code/.origin-main-sha`. For a PR head or uncommitted work, use `git grep` / `git show <sha>:<path>` instead.\n- **Search is lexical (BM25).** Use the words that appear in the code. Dotted identifiers such as `core.hooksPath` match as one token.\n- **Never index:**\n  - `eval/`\n  - held-out tasks or payloads\n  - credentials, or `~/.nexus`, `~/.codex` or `~/.claude` state\n\n  Index only folders you are allowed to read, under a new prefix that doesn't start with an existing one.\n- **Never delete or replace indices you didn't create.**\n- **Field reports are allowed for public/open-source work.** Preview with `xerj feedback --dry-run`, then `--submit`. Keep private data, paths of private repos and secrets out of them.\n- **Don't use `rerank`.** It sends document text to a third party.\n\n--- project-doc ---\n\n# Project Guidelines & Agent Instructions\n\n## Commands\n- Build: `make build` or `cargo build` or `npm run build`\n- Test: `make test` or `cargo test` or `npm test`\n- Lint: `cargo clippy` or `npm run lint`\n\n## Code Conventions\n- Maintain documentation integrity and keep existing comments.\n- Always run tests after making changes to verify correctness.\n- Keep functions modular and clearly typed.\n\n## Entire CLI\n- Set `ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file` in the environment before every `entire` command (for example, run `export ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file` first).\n\n## v1.0.0 work and concurrent agents\n- The v1.0.0 plan is in `docs/v1.0.0/` (start at `docs/v1.0.0/README.md`). Implement one claimed PR slice at a time, within the safe change boundary in its plan.\n- When more than one agent may be working, follow `docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`. In short:\n  - Claim the slice atomically under `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/`.\n  - Use one worktree and branch per slice; never edit `~/nexus-code` directly.\n  - Isolate `HOME` for every test or probe run.\n  - Claim hot files before editing them.\n  - Take the `GATEWAY` claim for any inference run.\n  - Never use `pkill -f`.\n  - Check `git log` for foreign commits before every commit.\n  - Leave push, tag and publish to the owner.\n\n<!-- entire-agent:begin -->\nRead .entire/agent-guide.md for this repository's workflow, source inspection, and verification guidance.\n@.entire/agent-guide.md\n<!-- entire-agent:end -->\n"},"apps_instructions":false,"collaboration_mode":{"mode":"default","model":"gpt-6-luna","instructions":"afcdf1ff905fb4e61ff4d6d89af089dbda3d5e4e"},"context_window_guidance":"","environments":{"environments":{"local":{"cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","status":"available","shell":"zsh"}},"current_date":"2026-11-03","timezone":"Etc/UTC","filesystem":"<filesystem><workspace_roots><root>/home/mike/nexus-code</root></workspace_roots><permission_profile type=\"disabled\"><file_system type=\"unrestricted\" /></permission_profile></filesystem>","subagents":"<agent name=\"/root/release_gate_audit\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/review_delta\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/roadmap_next\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/roadmap_status_audit\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/suite_state_audit\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/v112_gate_matrix\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/v112_next_slice_audit\" />\n<agent name=\"/root/v112_release_publication_audit\" />"},"environments_instructions":false,"git_attribution":false,"host_skills":{"body":"\n## Skills\nA skill is a set of local instructions to follow that is stored in a `SKILL.md` file. Below is the list of skills that can be used. Each entry includes a name, description, and a short path that can be expanded into an absolute path using the skill roots table.\n### Skill roots\n- `r0` = `/home/mike/.codex/skills`\n- `r1` = `/home/mike/.agents/skills`\n- `r2` = `/home/mike/.codex/skills/.system`\n- `r3` = `/home/mike/.codex/plugins/cache/claude-mem-local/claude-mem/15.8.1/skills`\n- `r4` = `/home/mike/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-bundled`\n- `r5` = `/home/mike/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote`\n- `r6` = `/home/mike/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/sites/1.1.2/skills`