{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:20:17.163Z","ordinal":78239,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a1a2da-e60b-7191-ba47-0fa76e64b2d1","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Deliverables: write a deck, report, page or other file the person asked for as a file and attach it as work_product before you finish. When you stop, claude-mem copies each attached file (and any deck, document, page, image or spreadsheet you wrote outside the source tree) into this project's deliverables bucket, ~/.claude-mem/deliverables/<project>/, and links it on the request's card in My Work.\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- ...793 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-11-03 7:20pm UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 50 obs (15,855t read) | 71,101t work | 78% savings\n\n### Nov 2, 2026\nS2134 v1.1.2 Release Scope Reconciliation and WP-1103 Qualification Gate — PLAN Phase with Concurrent Test Blocker (Nov 2, 12:21 PM)\nS2146 v1.1.2 Release — WP-1103 AC2 Mount-View Test Implementation, Source Review Approval, Release Docs Integration, and External Suite Monitoring (Nov 2, 12:39 PM)\nS2149 v1.1.2 Release — WP-1103 Exact-Source Qualification Gate: Waiting for Shared Test Host to Clear (Nov 2, 1:16 PM)\nS2150 v1.1.2 Release — WP-1103 Exact-Source Qualification Gate Blocked by Two External PR396 Test Streams (Nov 2, 1:35 PM)\nS2151 v1.1.2 Release — Goal Formally Blocked by Shared Test Host Contention, Awaiting External Test Stream Clearance (Nov 2, 1:45 PM)\n### Nov 3, 2026\n29174 5:28p ◆ Regression Test Added — CERI RunManifest harnessVersion Must Match Runtime Build Identity Version\n29175 5:29p ✓ CERI E2E harnessVersion Regression Test Confirmed RED — TDD Red Phase Complete\n29176 \" ● harnessVersion Hardcode Fixed — runner.ts Now Derives Version from getBuildIdentity(), Test Fixture Updated to rc.2\n29177 5:30p ✓ Qualification Record Corrected — Roadmap Items 3–7 Status Corrected, CERI Provenance Gap Disclosed\n29178 \" ● CERI harnessVersion Fix Confirmed Green — 3/3 Tests Pass, TDD Cycle Complete\n29179 \" ✓ Qualification Record Status Downgraded — RC2 Requalification Required After CERI Provenance Fix\n29180 5:31p ✓ v1.1.2 Work State Updated — Peer Review Surfaced Three Issues, All Corrected, Full make test Now Running\n29182 6:03p ○ jbd2 Journal Stall Detected in Post-CERI make test Run\n29183 6:05p ○ jbd2 Stall Resolved — Post-CERI Suite Resumed at Line 7370\n29184 6:08p ○ Inference Provider HTTP 500 During Post-CERI Suite Run\n29185 6:18p ✓ Post-CERI make test Completed — 2314 Pass / 0 Fail / 5 Skip\n29186 \" ✓ Tenth make test Run Launched — Post-CERI Log Overwritten for Fresh Run\n29187 \" ✓ Post-CERI make test Log SHA-256 Captured — All Gates Passed\n29188 \" ○ v1.1.2 Qualification Record Current State — RC2 Requalification Pending After CERI Fix\n29189 6:19p ✓ v1.1.2 Qualification Record Updated — Post-CERI RC2 Source Gates Marked Passed\n29190 \" ✓ Security Gates Re-Run on Complete Post-CERI Diff\n29191 \" ✓ Post-CERI Security Gates Passed — Final SHA-256s Captured\n29192 \" ✓ SUITE Claim Released — Post-CERI RC2 Qualification Gate Logged to Audit Trail\n29193 \" ✓ v1.1.2 Release Work State Updated — RC2 Source Gates Complete, Peer Re-Review Pending\n29194 \" ⚠ Encrypted Message Sent to /root/review_delta — Repeated Inter-Agent Communication Pattern\n29198 6:21p ✓ RC2 CERI Fix Committed — Commit e134dcd5 on v1/v112-wp1101-integration\n29199 \" ✓ Commit e134dcd5 Full Metadata — Parent f6d474a4, Approved by /root/review_delta\n29200 \" ○ Three Root Agent Results Retrieved — release_gate_audit, review_delta, roadmap_next All Completed\n29201 \" ✓ All RC2 File Claims Released — 10 Claims Logged to Audit Trail\n29202 \" ✓ v1.1.2 Release Work State Updated — Source Qualification Done, Artifact Production Next\n29203 6:22p ✓ RC2 Binary Rebuilt on Exact Commit e134dcd5 — Version 1.1.2-rc.2 Confirmed\n29204 6:23p ✓ Exact-Commit make test Started — New Log /tmp/v112-rc2-exact-make-test.log\n29207 6:42p ○ jbd2 Stall and Inference Failover During Exact-Commit Suite Run\n29209 7:09p ✓ Exact-Commit make test Completed — 2314 Pass / 0 Fail / 5 Skip, Security Gates Running\n29210 \" ✓ SUITE Claim Re-Acquired and Second Exact-Commit make test Started\n29211 7:10p ✓ First Exact-Commit make test SHA-256 Captured — All Security Gates Passed\n29212 \" ✓ SUITE Claim Released — First Exact-Commit Qualification Gate Logged to Audit Trail\n29213 \" ✓ RC2 Exact-Commit Source Gates Passed — Work State Updated\n29214 \" ○ Qualification Record Pre-Update State — RC2 Source Gates Passed, Artifact Gates Still Open\n29215 \" ✓ Qualification Record Updated to Exact Commit e134dcd5 Evidence\n29216 7:11p ✓ Security Gates Re-Run After Qualification Record Doc Update\n29217 \" ⚷ Third Encrypted Message Sent to /root/review_delta Agent\n29219 7:12p ⚖ RC2 Package Build Will Use Separate Clean Worktree at e134dcd5\n29220 \" ○ Clean Package Worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-rc2-package Already Exists at e134dcd5\n29221 7:13p ○ RC2 Package Build Already Running — Cargo Compilation in Progress\n29222 \" ○ RC2 Package Build Process Details — Pinned Rust 1.95.0 in Docker, No Errors\n29223 7:15p ○ RC2 Package Build Progressed to Node Stage — Rust Compilation Complete\n29224 \" ○ RC2 Package Build Environment Variables — Pinned Image SHA and Isolated Home Dirs\n29225 \" ◆ RC2 Package Archive Build Complete — First Archive Produced with Full SBOM\n29226 7:19p ◆ RC2 Archive Reproducibility Confirmed — Both Builds Produce Identical SHA-256\n29227 \" ○ RC2 Archive Contents and Compatibility Metadata Verified\n29228 \" ○ install.sh Pre-Install Self-Test and Compatibility Validation Logic Confirmed\n29229 \" ○ install.sh Requirements and Terminal Acceptance Gate Structure\n29230 \" ○ install.sh Download and Attestation Flow — GitHub API Version Resolution with Rate-Limit Handling\n29231 \" ○ package_runtime.test.mjs Structure — Eval Runtime File Allowlist and Evidence Schema Verified\n\nAccess 71k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only. Worker runtime: use Smart search by default: follow the mem-search skill in three steps—search({query, project}) for an index, timeline({anchor}) for context around relevant results, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records you choose after reviewing the index and context. Do not use auto or guided modes. Optional Dumb search, dumb_search({query, project}): Doesn’t reason about the results. Fast, but shallow. Use Smart for reliable recall. A hosted read-only connector may expose searches without write tools; do not call a missing write tool.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793733617.1636229,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"],"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"harness","hook":true}}]}}}
