\\nimport assert from \\\"node:assert/strict\\\";\\nimport fs from \\\"node:fs\\\";\\nimport os from \\\"node:os\\\";\\nimport path from \\\"node:path\\\";\\nimport { test } from \\\"node:test\\\";\\nimport http from \\\"node:http\\\";\\nimport { spawn, spawnSync } from \\\"node:child_process\\\";\\nimport { createHash } from \\\"node:crypto\\\";\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \\\"node:url\\\";\\nimport { stageEvaluatorRuntime, EVAL_RUNTIME_FILES } from \\\"../scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs\\\";\\n\\nconst expectedRuntimeFiles = [\\n  \\\"eval/run.mjs\\\", \\\"eval/validate.mjs\\\", \\\"eval/t4_fixtures.mjs\\\", \\\"eval/isolate.mjs\\\",\\n  \\\"eval/hide_oracle.cjs\\\", \\\"eval/hide_oracle.py\\\", \\\"eval/unlink_then_exec.sh\\\",\\n  \\\"eval/agent_sandbox.mjs\\\", \\\"eval/model_proxy.mjs\\\", \\\"eval/score.mjs\\\", \\\"eval/dataset.mjs\\\",\\n  \\\"eval/runner_integrity.mjs\\\", \\\"eval/runner_api.mjs\\\", \\\"eval/oracle.mjs\\\", \\\"eval/infra.mjs\\\",\\n  \\\"eval/workspace.mjs\\\", \\\"eval/resources.mjs\\\", \\\"eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs\\\", \\\"eval/t3.mjs\\\",\\n  \\\"eval/hardened_check.mjs\\\", \\\"eval/toolchain-versions.json\\\", \\\"eval/scan-compiler-exposure.mjs\\\",\\n  \\\"eval/evaluators/code/index.mjs\\\",\\n  \\\"eval/evaluators/code/syntax_ast.mjs\\\",\\n  \\\"eval/evaluators/code/build.mjs\\\",\\n  \\\"eval/evaluators/code/typecheck_clean.mjs\\\",\\n  \\\"eval/evaluators/code/diff_boundary.mjs\\\",\\n  \\\"eval/evaluators/code/runner.mjs\\\",\\n  \\\"eval/evaluators/code/json_repair_rate.mjs\\\",\\n  \\\"eval/evaluators/code/parsers.mjs\\\",\\n  \\\"eval/evaluators/code/command.mjs\\\",\\n  \\\"eval/evaluators/code/result.mjs\\\",\\n  \\\"eval/evaluators/code/README.md\\\",\\n];\\n\\ntest(\\\"installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance\\\", {\\n  skip: process.env.NEXUS_PACKAGE_ARCHIVE && process.env.NEXUS_PACKAGE_INSTALL_ROOT && process.env.NEXUS_ACCEPTANCE_EVIDENCE_PATH\\n    ? false\\n    : \\\"set exact package archive, safe install root and evidence paths to run installed-candidate acceptance\\\",\\n  timeout: 180_000,\\n}, async () => {\\n  const packageArchive = fs.realpathSync(process.env.NEXUS_PACKAGE_ARCHIVE);\\n  const installRoot = path.resolve(process.env.NEXUS_PACKAGE_INSTALL_ROOT);\\n  const evidencePath = process.env.NEXUS_ACCEPTANCE_EVIDENCE_PATH;\\n  const packageArchiveSha256 = createHash(\\\"sha256\\\").update(fs.readFileSync(packageArchive)).digest(\\\"hex\\\");\\n  assert.equal(path.basename(evidencePath).startsWith(`acceptance-${packageArchiveSha256.slice(0, 12)}`), true, \\\"acceptance evidence must be candidate-specific\\\");\\n  assert.equal(fs.existsSync(evidencePath), false, \\\"candidate evidence is immutable and must not overwrite an earlier run\\\");\\n  const sourceRoot = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \\\"..\\\");\\n  assert.equal(installRoot === \\\"/tmp\\\" || installRoot.startsWith(\\\"/tmp/\\\") || installRoot === \\\"/var/tmp\\\" || installRoot.startsWith(\\\"/var/tmp/\\\"), false, \\\"candidate runtime must be installed outside protected temporary roots\\\");\\n  assert.equal(installRoot === sourceRoot || installRoot.startsWith(`${sourceRoot}${path.sep}`), false, \\\"candidate install root must be outside the source checkout\\\");\\n  fs.mkdirSync(installRoot, { recursive: true });\\n  assert.deepEqual(fs.readdirSync(installRoot), [], \\\"candidate install root must be empty\\\");\\n  const listing = spawnSync(\\\"tar\\\", [\\\"-tzf\\\", packageArchive], { encoding: \\\"utf8\\\" });\\n  assert.equal(listing.status, 0, listing.stderr);\\n  assert.ok(listing.stdout.split(\\\"\\\\n\\\").filter(Boolean).every((entry) => entry.startsWith(\\\"nexus/\\\") && !entry.split(\\\"/\\\").includes(\\\"..\\\")), \\\"candidate archive must contain only the nexus/ package root\\\");\\n  const extracted = spawnSync(\\\"tar\\\", [\\\"-xzf\\\", packageArchive, \\\"-C\\\", installRoot], { encoding: \\\"utf8\\\" });\\n  assert.equal(extracted.status, 0, extracted.stderr);\\n  const packageRoot = fs.realpathSync(path.join(installRoot, \\\"nexus\\\"));\\n  const outside = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \\\"nexus-benchmark-acceptance-\\\"));\\n  const dataset = path.join(outside, \\\"dataset\\\");\\n  fs.cpSync(path.join(sourceRoot, \\\"eval/datasets/core-v1\\\"), dataset, { recursive: true });\\n  const manifestPath = path.join(dataset, \\\"manifest.json\\\");\\n  const manifestBytes = fs.readFileSync(manifestPath);\\n  const manifest = JSON.parse(manifestBytes.toString(\\\"utf8\\\"));\\n  const manifestSha256 = createHash(\\\"sha256\\\").update(manifestBytes).digest(\\\"hex\\\");\\n  const examples = fs.readFileSync(path.join(sourceRoot, \\\"eval/datasets/core-v1/examples.jsonl\\\"), \\\"utf8\\\")\\n    .split(\\\"\\\\n\\\").filter(Boolean).map((line) => JSON.parse(line));\\n  const oracles = fs.readFileSync(path.join(sourceRoot, \\\"eval/datasets/core-v1/oracles.jsonl\\\"), \\\"utf8\\\")\\n    .split(\\\"\\\\n\\\").filter(Boolean).map((line) => JSON.parse(line));\\n  const oracleById = new Map(oracles.map((oracle) => [oracle.id, oracle]));\\n  const benchmark = examples.filter((example) => example.split === \\\"benchmark\\\");\\n  const expectedIds = benchmark.map((example) => example.id).sort();\\n  assert.equal(expectedIds.length, manifest.splits.benchmark.count);\\n  const requests = [];\\n  const server = http.createServer((req, res) => {…2612 tokens truncated…  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dataset, \\\"examples.jsonl\\\"), examples);\\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dataset, \\\"oracles.jsonl\\\"), oracles);\\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dataset, \\\"manifest.json\\\"), `${JSON.stringify({\\n      schemaVersion: 1,\\n      name: \\\"empty-package-smoke\\\",\\n      version: \\\"1.0.0\\\",\\n      domains: [],\\n      splits: { regression: { count: 0 }, benchmark: { count: 0 } },\\n      files: {\\n        \\\"examples.jsonl\\\": createHash(\\\"sha256\\\").update(examples).digest(\\\"hex\\\"),\\n        \\\"oracles.jsonl\\\": createHash(\\\"sha256\\\").update(oracles).digest(\\\"hex\\\"),\\n      },\\n      tasks: {},\\n    }, null, 2)}\\\\n`);\\n\\n    const launcher = path.join(packageRoot, \\\"bin\\\", \\\"nexus\\\");\\n    const help = spawnSync(launcher, [\\\"eval\\\", \\\"--help\\\"], {\\n      cwd: outside,\\n      encoding: \\\"utf8\\\",\\n M docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\\ne134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd\\ndiff --git a/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md b/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\\nindex 15387c54..d65edbd1 100644\\n--- a/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\\n+++ b/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\\n # Nexus Code v1.1.2 Qualification Record\\n \\n **Status as of 2026-11-03: corrected RC2 source gates passed; artifact, installed-candidate, and publication qualification remain open.**\\n-This record tracks the v1.1.2 candidate on branch `v1/v112-wp1101-integration`, covering the full WP-1101 through WP-1108 scope and release gates G1.1-1 through G1.1-5 in accordance with the [v1.1.0 roadmap](../v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md) and [v1.1.2 roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md). The package metadata is synchronized at `1.1.2-rc.2`. After correcting CERI provenance to use the package build identity, `make test` passed 2,314 of 2,319 tests with 0 failures and 5 skips, including the terminal process-scope fixtures; the security lifecycle gates passed and `make build` passed (including TypeScript type checking). Full-suite log SHA-256: `39cad26938be30dbb4b073a4d93e62a80aa920789e751cccba5465795eb362bd`. The regression test was RED against the old RC1 provenance and its focused green run passed 3/3 tests (log SHA-256 `61e0eab4c25d6071a8fb4b22f541a3248759bc0997c0b1124183ead05531a0b4`). The corrected candidate is based on source commit `f6d474a4` with RC2 package metadata and the CERI provenance fix; a clean exact commit build and fresh RC2 archive are still required.\\n+This record tracks the v1.1.2 candidate on branch `v1/v112-wp1101-integration`, covering the full WP-1101 through WP-1108 scope and release gates G1.1-1 through G1.1-5 in accordance with the [v1.1.0 roadmap](../v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md) and [v1.1.2 roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md). The package metadata is synchronized at `1.1.2-rc.2`. On clean commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd`, `make build` passed and the CLI reported `1.1.2-rc.2 (e134dcd51034, v1/v112-wp1101-integration)`. The exact-commit `make test` passed 2,314 of 2,319 tests with 0 failures and 5 skips; terminal process-scope fixtures and all security lifecycle gates passed. Full-suite log SHA-256: `716a39d0fe766a3ee3e9defcefa010edb1b02c3c7a64faa570096d8b8b125963`. The CERI regression test failed against the old RC1 provenance and then passed 3/3 tests (green log SHA-256 `61e0eab4c25d6071a8fb4b22f541a3248759bc0997c0b1124183ead05531a0b4`). A fresh RC2 archive and installed-candidate qualification remain required.\\n \\n The v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files. v1.1.1 is the immutable published predecessor. The earlier RC1 package archive is historical and is not eligible for release. The current source candidate is being advanced to RC2; no RC2 archive or installed-candidate evidence has been produced yet.\\n \\n@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@ The candidate branch `v1/v112-wp1101-integration` contains the WP-1101–WP-1108\\n \\n | Package | Required outcome | Observed evidence | Status | Evidence details |\\n |---|---|---|---|---|\\n-| WP-1101 — OpenTelemetry local tracing | Local GenAI spans for turns, model requests, tools, and compactions; credentials protected and trace output confined. | Lifecycle instrumentation integrated in commit `97945557`, extending the existing local recorder. Public worktree-backed turns emit exactly one turn span; all four direct model request sites, tool dispatch, and compaction paths are traced with payload-free attributes. | **PASSED** | Fresh independent review APPROVED. The corrected RC2 source suite passed 2,314/0/5 on the candidate based on `f6d474a4`; its full log SHA-256 is `39cad26938be30dbb4b073a4d93e62a80aa920789e751cccba5465795eb362bd`. Earlier WP-1101 integration evidence summary SHA-256 `e795474bab9a71c0ecd0bdedffef8db5ceeaff81935ab3f7edbb964c7d741e17`. |\\n+| WP-1101 — OpenTelemetry local tracing | Local GenAI spans for turns, model requests, tools, and compactions; credentials protected and trace output confined. | Lifecycle instrumentation integrated in commit `97945557`, extending the existing local recorder. Public worktree-backed turns emit exactly one turn span; all four direct model request sites, tool dispatch, and compaction paths are traced with payload-free attributes. | **PASSED** | Fresh independent review APPROVED. Exact clean RC2 commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd` passed 2,314/0/5; suite log SHA-256 `716a39d0fe766a3ee3e9defcefa010edb1b02c3c7a64faa570096d8b8b125963`. Earlier WP-1101 integration evidence summary SHA-256 `e795474bab9a71c0ecd0bdedffef8db5ceeaff81935ab3f7edbb964c7d741e17`. |\\n | WP-1102 — Flight recorder credential redaction | Zero-leak sanitization across traces, CLI errors, and debug journals. | Integrated in commit `9c1926e1`. Comprehensive regex + token redactor applied across all flight recorder sinks. | **PASSED** | Validated in `cli/test/*_redaction.test.ts` (22/22 passed across all sinks and adversarial fixtures). |\\n | WP-1103 — Versioned evaluation datasets | Versioned datasets with separate examples/oracles and regression/benchmark splits; candidate prompts cannot access oracles. | Integrated in commit `11f41ed0`. Serialized complete CLI suite passed (2,251 tests). Process-scope fixtures passed with zero orphaned processes. 6-task installed acceptance passed. | **PASSED** | Manifest SHA-256 `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`. Evidence preserved in `docs/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-28d79f3b0f4d.json`. |\\n | WP-1104 — Standalone `nexus eval` | Packaged command supports dataset selection, run count, isolated home, and structured score output. | Integrated in commit `11f41ed0`. Verified package parity and standalone CLI execution outside repository checkout. | **PASSED** | Validated in `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` (5/5 passed). Verified with isolated HOME, dataset selection, and structured scoring. |\\n@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@ The candidate branch `v1/v112-wp1101-integration` contains the WP-1101–WP-1108\\n | G1.1-2 — Dataset decoupling | All benchmark tasks execute and no oracle data reaches candidate prompts; exact candidate and process-scope evidence retained. | Prior six-task package evidence is bound to the historical `9c1926e1` archive, not source `97945557`. Rebuild and rerun installed-candidate acceptance. | **REQUALIFICATION REQUIRED** |\\n | G1.1-3 — CLI parity | Packaged `nexus eval` works without developer dependencies on the exact release candidate. | Prior package parity evidence predates `97945557`; rebuild the archive and rerun standalone CLI parity on the new package. | **REQUALIFICATION REQUIRED** |\\n | G1.1-4 — Constrained decoding | At least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across supported provider endpoints. | Source grammar tests passed in the final-source suite; bind the supported-endpoint metric to the rebuilt release candidate. | **SOURCE PASSED; package qualification pending** |\\n-| G1.1-5 — Zero technical debt | Zero deprecated/unmaintained packages, zero CodeQL alerts and compiler warnings, plus required suite/PTY, cargo-deny, npm scans, reproducibility, and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants. | Corrected RC2 full suite, TypeScript build, npm/cargo security scans, and terminal process-scope fixtures passed. Package checksums, SBOM, installer, reproducibility, and CLI option compatibility remain pending for the fresh archive. | **SOURCE GATES PASSED; artifact gates pending** |\\n+| G1.1-5 — Zero technical debt | Zero deprecated/unmaintained packages, zero CodeQL alerts and compiler warnings, plus required suite/PTY, cargo-deny, npm scans, reproducibility, and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants. | On exact commit `e134dcd5`, full suite, TypeScript build, npm/cargo security scans, and terminal process-scope fixtures passed. Package checksums, SBOM, installer, reproducibility, and CLI option compatibility remain pending for the fresh archive. | **SOURCE GATES PASSED; artifact gates pending** |\\n \\n ## Historical RC1 artifact (not release-qualified)\\n \\n@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@ The exact release candidate distribution archive was built using the approved di\\n - [ ] All WP-1101–WP-1108 acceptance evidence and test suites are bound to the final candidate.\\n - [ ] Current v1.1.2 roadmap items and release gates are qualified on the final candidate.\\n - [x] Prior RC2 full source suite, security lifecycle scans, `make build`/TypeScript type build, and terminal process-scope acceptance passed before the CERI provenance correction.\\n-- [x] Corrected RC2 full source suite, security scans, and type build passed on the source candidate based on `f6d474a4`; rerun once more on the clean commit that binds the final artifact.\\n+- [x] Corrected RC2 full source suite, security scans, and type build passed on exact clean commit `e134dcd5103446f97e341059b54d85883e4c52fd`.\\n - [ ] Release scans, package checksums, SBOM, installer behavior, and reproducibility verified for the final archive.\\n - [ ] CLI option compatibility and installed-candidate acceptance verified for the final archive.\\n - [ ] Acceptance evidence and qualification record committed for the final candidate.\\n\"},{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Saved to \\\"v1.1.2-release\\\" in nexus-code. Still open in it:\\n- ...10 more lines; read them with work_state_read\"}]}]"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793733633.5213459}},"metadata":{"client_authored